{
  "task_description": "{'component_name': 'Main Container for YouthSync Suite', 'description': 'Primary container for YouthSync Suite implementation: DevAssist AI is a modern, dark-themed React web application for students and young adults, featuring three productivity tools: GradeBoost (CGPA calculator), SplitMate (bill splitter), and FocusFlow (Pomodoro timer). The landing page showcases three glowing, interactive icons for each tool, routing to dedicated pages with responsive, visually engaging UIs. Each tool page includes dynamic forms, real-time feedback (charts/timers), and is optimized for users aged 18–23. Built with React.js, React Router DOM, and Tailwind CSS, the app emphasizes clean architecture, input validation, and a youthful, modern aesthetic.', 'framework': 'react', 'platform': 'web', 'container': '{\n  "name": "ColorCraft frontend Container",\n  "features": [\n    {\n      "name": "GradeBoost",\n      "description": "Build a CGPA Calculator tool where users can:  Input subjects dynamically with:  Grade (like S, A, B, C, D, E, F) via dropdown  Credit value via number input  On clicking \\u201cCalculate GPA\\u201d, it should:  Validate all fields are filled properly  Convert grades to grade points (S=10, A=9, ..., F=0)  Multiply grade point \\u00d7 credit for each subject  Compute GPA = Total Grade Points / Total Credits  Show the GPA result with:  A circular or linear progress bar  A text summary of performance  Provide:  A \\u201cReset\\u201d button to clear all input fields  Basic input validation (no negative credits, valid grades only)",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "SplitMate",\n      "description": "Build a bill splitting tool where users can:  Input total amount of the bill  Enter number of people to split between  Optionally:  Add individual names (for display)  Add custom percentage shares (default equal share)  On clicking \\u201cSplit Bill\\u201d, it should:  Calculate amount per person (or custom share)  Display each person\'s share in a card/list format  Include:  Input validation (e.g., zero/negative values not allowed)  A reset button to clear everything",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "FocusFlow",\n      "description": "Build a Pomodoro timer tool to help users focus. It should:  Let users start a 25-min Pomodoro timer with:  Optional custom time input (e.g., 30 or 45 mins)  A countdown display with minutes & seconds  Include:  Start, Pause, and Reset buttons  A progress circle or linear bar  Optional sound or alert when time ends  Add session tracking:  Show how many Pomodoros completed  Simple \\u201cFocus Summary\\u201d display",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    }\n  ],\n  "techStack": {\n    "frontend": [\n      "React JS"\n    ],\n    "backend": [\n      "None"\n    ],\n    "language": [\n      "JavaScript (ES6+)"\n    ]\n  },\n  "colors": {\n    "primary": "#18181b",\n    "secondary": "#27272a",\n    "accent": "#38bdf8"\n  },\n  "theme": "dark",\n  "layoutDescription": "The homepage features a dark background with three large, horizontally aligned, glowing circular icons (GradeBoost, SplitMate, FocusFlow) centered on the screen. On hover, each icon glows more intensely and scales up. Clicking an icon routes to its tool page via React Router. Each tool page has a clean, responsive layout: GradeBoost uses forms and a circular progress indicator; SplitMate uses forms and a pie chart or summary; FocusFlow uses timer controls and a circular countdown. All pages use Tailwind CSS for styling, spacing, and animations, with a clear folder structure (/components, /pages, /assets).\\n\\nAll tools should be:\\nResponsive\\n\\nUse Tailwind CSS\\n\\nImplement React Router DOM for navigation\\n\\nMaintain a consistent UI theme"\n}'}",
